Decision: HOLD DECK at conviction 4, core position. It is already at its conviction size, so it doesn't need an ADD.

research/DECK/2026-11-07-evaluation.md
OK research/DECK/2026-11-07-evaluation.md Bear case=139 Bull case=128 decision=HOLD

- **Thesis unchanged:** gross margin (58.9%) and operating margin (23.6%) are near five-year highs, and free cash flow still covers net income about 1:1. P/E, EV/EBITDA and P/FCF are all below their five-year lows. The price implies sales shrinking (-1.2% next year), while guidance still points to growth.
- **What keeps it at 4:** management cut the sales outlook on 2026-10-22, and rivals are discounting hard. Margins are helped by one-off tariff refunds. ROIC has fallen to 71.9% from 104.4%, and short interest is rising.
- **Triggers changed:** I replaced the old "ROIC below 70%" trigger, which is close to firing on today's 71.9%. The new ones are FCF margin below 12% and revenue falling for two quarters in a row. The gross margin (55%) and operating margin (20%) triggers stay. Moving a trigger that is about to fire is a judgement call, so look at this one before you accept the decision.
- **Scenarios over 12 months:** bull 130 (25%), base 105 (50%), bear 65 (25%), against a close of 86.71. The base is a little below the mechanical fair value of 112.86 because of the tariff refunds.
- **Entry price set to null:** the default (base fair value × 0.8, about 90) is above today's price, which the rule doesn't allow. Price isn't what is blocking an ADD. The checker passed with null.
- **Macro:** context only, so it didn't change the decision.
